cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PARC-Delta Lab: p-11B alpha-channeling research model and PDX-1 test-stand concept study"
abstract: >-
  An open, reproducible research codebase combining PARC-Delta v1.6, an exploratory
  p-11B alpha-channeling model (linear and finite-k_parallel ion-Bernstein-wave kinetics,
  sequential p-11B alpha birth kinematics, conserving Coulomb Monte Carlo and Rosenbluth,
  Takizuka-Abe and Nanbu alpha slowing-down), with PDX-1, a concept linear magnetized
  test stand designed, simulated and rendered from a single parameter file. Concept study
  only; no claim of fusion gain or net power.
authors:
  - given-names: "Aditya"
    alias: "sinhaaditya5"
version: "1.6.0"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sinhaaditya5/PARC-Delta-Lab"
keywords:
  - fusion
  - proton-boron
  - p-B11
  - alpha channeling
  - ion Bernstein wave
  - Fokker-Planck
  - Coulomb collisions
  - magnetic mirror
  - plasma physics
  - reproducible research
